{"requirements":[{"id":"prometheus-replicas-host-metrics","requirement":"Run independent Prometheus replicas on node1 and node2 and collect host metrics from all four managed nodes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both replicas were active, enabled, ready, independently labeled, and connected as separate Thanos sidecars. Each reported exactly four configured node targets with 4/4 healthy, persistent TSDB blocks, successful uploads, and zero upload failures. Both replicas also recovered fully after separate OS restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60a3fd9bbfd94004","cmd-46574634904c418e","cmd-47f72e51bb03481a","cmd-87ddc23966e54282","cmd-d123eb97bdd84cb7","cmd-9d724baad8b64a86","cmd-09a95f803a594aec","cmd-198c63b1272a4a2f","cmd-4ef4dc3f22e64089","cmd-4a816374bab34127","cmd-116761364401434a","cmd-3a668b00747243e1","cmd-68d7386a00dc468e","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"thanos-services-node3","requirement":"Provide Thanos Query, Store Gateway, and Compactor on node3, with queries available on port 10902.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Query, Store Gateway, and Compactor were active, enabled, and ready on node3. Query had three healthy store connections, Store loaded object-store blocks, Compactor completed iterations without halting, and bucket verification completed successfully. The complete service and query state recovered after node3 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1d36b28d9b2b4eea","cmd-47f72e51bb03481a","cmd-9da9e5c7f9694f0a","cmd-756cbbcdf3ee47ae","cmd-90b0a63034e1489a","cmd-8389f8a671374cf6","global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"authenticated-https-object-store","requirement":"Provide an authenticated HTTPS object store at node4:9000 using bucket thanos-metrics and data under /srv/thanos-objectstore.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The MinIO unit explicitly used port 9000, TLS certificates, and /srv/thanos-objectstore. Final probes showed successful certificate-validated HTTPS readiness, authenticated access to thanos-metrics, anonymous denial with HTTP 403, nine persisted metadata objects, and the required data-directory ownership. Authentication, objects, and service state recovered after node4 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bbdfe9e8c24c46e9","cmd-8af9686ee22f4048","cmd-edfebebb396245c3","cmd-51e8a6152e944467","cmd-9a292e80ba0c4922","cmd-cb68f931ea1140cf","cmd-9fce62ca25a74c6a","global:before_prepare:node4:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"node3-object-store-variables","requirement":"Place the object-store access variables in /root/thanos-objectstore.env on node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The file was created from the object-store variables with root ownership and mode 600. Its protected presence was observed before and after node3's restart, while node3 successfully authenticated to and verified the object store.","evidence_ids":["cmd-20ae5fbffe8e41a7","cmd-9f8d5590b0e24ab3","cmd-9da9e5c7f9694f0a","cmd-8389f8a671374cf6","cmd-47f72e51bb03481a"]},{"id":"deduplication-and-prometheus-failover","requirement":"Queries on node3:10902 must deduplicate replicas and continue returning current and historical results when either Prometheus server is unavailable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The healthy baseline returned four fresh host series with replica labels removed and historical results for both replicas. During a confirmed node1 Prometheus-and-sidecar outage, Query remained ready, returned four fresh deduplicated series, and returned node1-labeled stored history; full node1 and store membership then recovered. The same bounded transition succeeded independently for node2, including node2-labeled history and full recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7cf609d66de0454f","cmd-57b6e36575fa4005","cmd-8e63a64f0caf403e","cmd-40f44c406f4342ee","cmd-086304d8274747f0","cmd-b448589e80a44e27","cmd-17e3f7e7490a4fdb","cmd-85d8dc90800f4909","cmd-e3726d7c85ba48b3"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.86,"summary":"Most mutations had clear implementation, verification, restoration, or mandatory-restart roles, and the final snapshots showed no failed services or damaged dpkg state. Unnecessary retained exposure: cmd-f3a9d18598c440fa and cmd-8e1a427e7b5446e3 enabled Prometheus's unauthenticated web lifecycle controls while binding port 9090 to all interfaces; no command used those controls, and the setting remained. Unnecessary retained residue: cmd-87ddc23966e54282, cmd-4ef4dc3f22e64089, cmd-9da9e5c7f9694f0a, and cmd-51e8a6152e944467 necessarily created persistent boot-ID markers for restart proof but did not clean them afterward. Unnecessary temporary-body mutation: cmd-51e8a6152e944467 wrote unused /tmp/pre-restart-anonymous, which was cleared by the ensuing reboot; cmd-9fce62ca25a74c6a and cmd-edfebebb396245c3 wrote unused /tmp/post-restart-anonymous and /tmp/final-anonymous, both retained and confirmed by the final snapshot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f3a9d18598c440fa","cmd-8e1a427e7b5446e3","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","cmd-87ddc23966e54282","cmd-4ef4dc3f22e64089","cmd-9da9e5c7f9694f0a","cmd-51e8a6152e944467","cmd-9a292e80ba0c4922","cmd-cb68f931ea1140cf","cmd-9fce62ca25a74c6a","cmd-edfebebb396245c3","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and bounded failover evidence. Separately, the provider-wide restart protocol is complete on all four nodes: every node has a healthy pre-restart state, explicit restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service, data, and cluster state. The command-level pre/post boot IDs exactly match the fixed baseline and after-executor boot observations.","limitations":["Failover was tested through brief, sequential single-Prometheus outages; the evidence does not measure sustained outage behavior, simultaneous failures, or performance under load, none of which was expressly required.","Historical persistence was probed at one timestamp and returned one matching stored series for each unavailable replica; it does not establish a long-term retention horizon.","Secret values were appropriately redacted, so final credential correctness is corroborated by their creation path and successful authenticated operations rather than literal value inspection.","The lifecycle collector does not inventory persistent application-data directories; retained boot-marker files are inferred from their writes, later reads, and the absence of cleanup in the complete command timeline."]}
